      "content": "hey, i'm helping out with a local community group and i need to write a speech for a town hall. the vibe is basically that people can't just sit on the sidelines anymore. i need something really powerful and morally uncompromising about why every single citizen has a direct moral obligation to show up and vote in every local election, even when the candidates are terrible or it feels pointless. can you help me draft a draft that makes it sound like a heavy civic duty? something that really hits home that not voting is a failure of character. thanks.",
